🚽 Test case: a STDROT_ANY parameter (slorp's) accepts any scalar/string
🚽 type, but not a pointer -- slorp has no notion of "read a pointer from
🚽 stdin". A pointer argument must be rejected statically, not silently
🚽 misinterpreted as whatever the generic scalar marshalling fallback
🚽 would have produced from the raw address.
skibidi main {
    rizz x = 5;
    rizz *p = &x;
    slorp(p);
    bussin 0;
}
